Whatever system call df uses to retrieve filesystem usage doesn't
include reserved-blocks, regardless of the capabilities of the user
calling it. Interestingly, if the superuser starts writing to a "full"
filesystem with available reserved blocks, df (or at least the
implementation on my box) will report negative free space for that
filesystem.

